  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nSo I noticed that when I open Homarr on my mobile device. 2 out of my 25 app are in their 'Media' category I created, but the other 3 categories I created become empty and all apps show up above the categories. I don't see anything in the logs that would indicate a problem, but I'm guessing this is all happening client side. \n\nI don't have any custom CSS. Everything was added through the web interface. I do have 3 layouts: small, medium, and large. And I do think that is the source of the problem. On the 'large' layout, it works as expected. If I resize to the medium layout, everything, except for those 2 apps, drop out of their respective category. \n\nThen I resized it so it gets the small layout, and manually added an app into a category, and that app stays in the category for small and large, and drops out again for medium. \n\nSo does that mean I have to categorize my apps separately for each layout? That doesn't make sense to me. Shouldn't the category an app belongs to stay the same no matter what the layout is?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI put all the details on how to reproduce in the bug description. \n\n### Impact\n\nThis makes Homarr a lot less usable on mobile. At the very least, it is a huge pain to have to recategorize all my apps for each layout. \n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version\n\n1.16.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
