      "created_at": "2025-04-23T18:23:45Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-04-23T18:23:45Z",
      "body": "Just my 2 cents. I really don't think that should be how it is designed. I could be wrong, but I'm thinking most people assign categories based on what the app does. Example, you might have one category that has media(stuff like Jellyfin or Plex). Another category might have infrastructure. Things like docker and uptime kuma. I really don't think most people are categorizing them differently on mobile vs desktop. And on top of that, there's no simple way to change the actual layout for the desktop from mobile. \n\nAnd what I would love to see, if it is even possible, is to just have one layout, and it automatically adjusts everything based on the screen size. Basically just try to keep the icons a certain size(or a range of size) and just resize things automatically. And option to have something like that instead of manually creating layouts for every size of screen I might use would be really nice. ",
