      "created_at": "2025-08-23T07:33:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-08-23T07:33:00Z",
      "body": "Actually, Homarr seems to remember all app -> dynamic section relations per breakpoint from before today/yesterday. I also moved some apps between sections and when I reduce the canvas size, not only the new ones jump out of their dynamic sections but also apps which I moved from one to another jump back to where they were before...\n\nIn my opinion that doesn't make sense. @simpat1zq is right. People assign apps to dynamic sections or categories based on function - or maybe physical location or topic. In any case, by criteria which don't change with the screen/canvas size.\nAnd I'm fairly sure, nobody wants to edit possibly multiple dashboards for multiple breakpoints. And keep multiple breakpoints updated at every change. That amount of configuration work would defeat the purpose of a dashboard app -> fast, simple access to a large number of services.",
