      "created_at": "2025-11-14T20:02:28Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-11-14T20:02:28Z",
      "body": "I'm not sure if this would be possible, but I think one way you might be able to handle this is to limit how small the icons can get in a particular layout. For example, I have my layout set to 9 columns. If I make the browser smaller(which basically simulates a smaller screen), then the icons keep getting smaller to a point that they are useless. But, if there were a setting that limits how small the icons can get, and instead simply reduces the number of columns to prevent them from getting too small, I really think it would work perfectly on any size screen. \n\nI'm not sure how hard that would be to implement or how well it would work, but I feel that if you can get something like that working then homarr would be great for people that use it across multiple devices. ",
      "author_association": "NONE",
