      "body": "i have the same issue. But it's not only on mobile.\nBelow are screenhots of my desktop Firefox 153.0.4 (64-bits)\n\nMy responsive layout settings\n\n- small, 0 , columns 4\n- medium, 600, columns 6\n- large, 1200, columns 10\n\n**Layed out good. Uses \"large\"**\n<img width=\"1267\" height=\"477\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a9983e8-c900-484f-a0ac-8d3c3d8ad540\" />\n\n**Faulty layed out. Uses \"medium\"**\n<img width=\"1041\" height=\"709\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/323f013e-29db-4eba-9124-b3d2d009f554\" />\n\n**Faulty layed out. Uses \"small\"**\n<img width=\"495\" height=\"663\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3b532731-be86-4986-bfa4-204c36e8aaf4\" />\n\n! The runtime behaviour even changes when i enter the layouts in reverse order, so starting with 'large'",
